-- title:
--   Euler characteristic additivity along a word of Cartier twists
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes, let $\iota : Y \to X$ be a morphism and let $y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper. Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $I_0,\dots,I_{m-1}$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on $X$ such that each $I_j$ is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has an affine open $U$ and an $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with the point in $X_f$ and $I_j$ on the affine basic open of $f$ generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and such that each inverse image $\iota^{-1}I_j$ on $Y$ is invertible in the same sense. Let $d : \{0,\dots,m-1\} \to \mathbb{N}$ be such that for each $j$ the composite of the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by $\iota^{-1}I_j$ with $y$ is finite and has rank $d_j$ at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$. Let $\mathrm{pos},\mathrm{neg} : \{0,\dots,m-1\} \to \mathbb{N}$, let $N$ be an $\mathcal{O}_X$-module which is invertible (every point has an open neighbourhood on which the restriction of $N$ is isomorphic to the structure sheaf), and let $\mathcal{W}$ consist of two affine opens $U_0,U_1$ of $Y$ with affine intersection and $U_0 \cup U_1 = Y$. For an $\mathcal{O}_Y$-module $M$ write $\chi(M) = \dim_k H^0 - \dim_k H^1$ for the two-term Čech complex of $M$ on $\mathcal{W}$, where $H^0$ is the kernel of the difference map $\Gamma(M,U_0) \times \Gamma(M,U_1) \to \Gamma(M,U_0 \cap U_1)$ and $H^1$ its cokernel, both as $k$-vector spaces. Then, with $W$ the right-nested fold over $j = 0,\dots,m-1$ of $M \mapsto (I_j^{\mathrm{pos}_j})^{\vee} \otimes I_j^{\mathrm{neg}_j} \otimes M$ applied to $N$ (here $I^n$ denotes the ideal sheaf viewed as a module, i.e. the kernel of the map from the structure sheaf to the pushforward of the structure sheaf of the subscheme it cuts out, and $(\cdot)^{\vee}$ its dual), one has $\chi(\iota^{*}W) = \chi(\iota^{*}N) + \sum_j (\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j)\, d_j$.
--
--   This is additivity of degree for twists by effective Cartier divisors, read through the two-chart Čech Euler characteristic on $Y$: twisting an invertible module by $\mathcal{O}(\mathrm{pos}_j Z_j - \mathrm{neg}_j Z_j)$ changes $\chi$ by $(\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j)\deg(Z_j|_Y)$. It is the multi-divisor form used when the divisor of a collection of sections of a relative curve is extended over a regular model, and is cited in the computation of Euler characteristics of folded twists on resolved models of modular curves and in the study of the relative Picard functor.
